  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "blandishments and sportive gestures. सदयं—such a man falls a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ready victim to their charms. वामनयना–mark the pun on वाम",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "which means ( 1 ) beautiful; ( 2 ) crooked, destructive.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 35. खर—rough. The moral is-Magnanimous persons",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "never become slaves of passions.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 36. हन्त—a particle expressive of joy. हरिणैः परिचयः—a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "favourite idea with the poet and referred to in many places.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "वृत्ति—Cf. supra sl. 27. हरभक्तिम्-स्पृहेरीप्सितः Pân. ईप्सितमात्रे इयं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "संज्ञा । प्रकर्षविवक्षायां तु परत्वात्कर्मसंज्ञा । पुष्पाणि स्पृहयति । Sid. Kau.—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "उपशान्त्येक whose minds are set on tranquillity alone ( i. e. who",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "are self-restrained. )",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 37. स्वादिष्ट—is superlative. Its use with the ablative is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "unusual. Construe—दैवी वाक् रसवतः अमृतात्मनः यत् मधुनः घृताच्च",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "स्वादिष्ठं रसवत् अक्षरं प्रस्रवति तेन &c. दवी वाक्—The Veda, especially",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the Upanishads which are chiefly concerned with Brahma. No",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "earthly enjoyments give that pleasure to a Yogin which the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "teaching of the Upanishads does. अमृता may also be taken",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "separately. The vedas are eternal धृति-support, sustenance. There",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "may also be here a reference to the divine speech of the poet",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "whose substratum is Rasa sending forth an immortal creation",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "sweeter than honey &c, .",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 39. करुणा, मैत्री, and प्रज्ञा (power of discernment), are here",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "called वधूजन—ladies who are desirable companions. शरणम्—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "protector, saviour. मणिमेखला a waist band set with jewels.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 40. The sl. describes the state of feelings of one in whom",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Vairâgya is produced. मन्थराः-(1) slow; (2) crooked. आस्था ear-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "nest desire. क्षीणः—wasted: has ceased. जगज्जाल—this net-work",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "of the world i. e. all its intricate and confounding incidents.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 41. प्रभाचोर—one that robs another of its brilliancy i. e.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "is as brilliant as that, possesses its brilliancy. Cf. सरोरुहद्युतिमुषः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Rat. I. अनया किमभिप्रेतम्—What can she have intended ? what is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "her object? वराकी—miserable, wretched; expresses pity. Also",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "sometimes used as a word of contempt.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
